<newsitem itemid="223825" id="root" date="1996-11-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Southern Electric H1 pretax profit falls.</title>
<headline>Southern Electric H1 pretax profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		34.3		   vs 33.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 12.9		   vs 11.3</p>
<p> Pretax		     112.2		  vs 118.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   782.4		  vs 734.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 102 to 120 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 119.2		  vs 111.9</p>
<p> Interest payable	 15.8		   vs 2.8</p>
<p> Tax			  23.5		   vs 27.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  88.7		   vs 91.7</p>
<p> Attributable	     88.7		   vs 91.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   March 4, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Feb 11, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Feb 3, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE: Southern Electric Plc is a regional electricity company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
